+# Round 2 review — round-1 fix commit
+
+## HIGH — src/OrderPricing.kt:17 — the round-1 slippage fix did not work
+`drift.equals(cap)` compares BigDecimal **scale as well as value**, so a cap of
+`0.10` does not match a drift of `0.1` and the boundary case silently reports
+out-of-cap. Round 1 claimed this fixed; it is not. Use `compareTo(cap) <= 0`.
+
+## HIGH — src/OrderPricing.kt:10 — round 1's new applyDiscount is off by 100x
+`subtotal.multiply(discountPercent)` applies the percentage as a raw multiplier
+with no division by 100. A `discountPercent` of `10` subtracts ten times the
+subtotal rather than ten percent of it, returning a large negative total. This
+defect was introduced by round 1's own fix commit.
+
+## Notes
+- `formatForDisplay` Double conversion and the literal `50` default were both
+  deferred in round 1 with recorded reasons; not re-raised here.
+- The `feeFor` null guard from round 1 is correct as applied.
